ts strategic location and robust fortifications made it a focal point in the power struggles of the region, particularly during the Maratha and British colonial eras. Notable figures associated with Jhansi include Rani Lakshmibai, who became an emblem of resistance against British rule during the Indian Rebellion of 1857, often referred to as the First War of Independence.

